'' THE ARGUMENTS REACH THE LINES ABOVE THE DIRECTIVE, because the restart re-reads
'' the file from the top rather than applying anything from where it was found.
'' Measured on fbc 1.20.0: '#ifdef FOO' BEFORE '#cmdline "-d FOO"' is taken on the
'' second pass, and fbc prints its '#print' output twice for the same reason.
''
'' The unparseable line is the assertion. It sits in the branch that is live only
'' while the symbol is undefined, so a run that did not restart reports a parse
'' error and a run that did never sees it. Pass one DOES report it -- and throws it
'' away unflushed, which is the other half of what this pins.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0

#if not defined( RETROSYMBOL )
    )))
#endif

#cmdline "-d RETROSYMBOL"

print "ok"
